  "review_findings_addressed": [
    "Magnitude-based Frobenius trimming could erase tiny divergent logarithms: endpoint-only strict evaluation and exact support admission; 10^-300 leading/later/cancellation adversaries tested.",
    "Normalization pads coefficient arrays beyond the uniformly known series order: true-order check and a private normalization-padding regression.",
    "Rounded root/basis cancellation cannot prove finite support: exact conservative all-lifted-direction admission occurs before numerical matching.",
    "Tiny exact positive exponents must not be rejected by a sampled-parameter genericity test: exact-rational endpoint path uses exact resonance decisions.",
    "Complex inverse cancellation can leave a few-bit imaginary component: outward rescale exact stored dyadic balls before native products; winding\u00b11 probes and endpoint regressions retain unchanged residual threshold.",
    "Bounded epsilon count and checked dimension*count preflight precede source pullback; bounded checked order growth and rollback tested."
  ],
  "initial_development_run": "Archived endpoints.log is the preceding13/15 run: winding residual metadata and rounded-root-cancellation failures were diagnosed and fixed. The initial private normalization-padding regression exposed that the order check needed to precede matching inversion; that failing log is retained separately. Final logs are authoritative.",
  "known_ignored_scope": "Existing explicitly ignored full13 prescribed-cache acceptance and optional native serialization profiling remain ignored. No new ignored tests, skips, or weakened assertions were added.",
  "limits": [
    "Coefficientwise limits after finite epsilon expansion; not symbolic dimensional-sector projection.",
    "Independent-profile comparisons plus propagated input uncertainty are estimates, not a global forward-error certificate.",
    "Exact support admission is sufficient and conservative for every lifted rational direction; valid correlated/constrained physical sectors may be rejected and require further work for full parity.",
    "Existing Fuchsian normalization, indicial-root, irregular-sector and resource limits remain explicit.",
    "Exact punctured-disk admission can conservatively reject larger valid matching domains.",
    "Rust prescribed endpoint routes are available; Python exposes the ordinary matching route.",
    "No claim of whole-project feature completeness, global CI green, or new publication physics acceptance."
  ],
